@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@token = REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_AUTHENTICATED_BEARER_TOKEN
@tenantId = REPLACE_WITH_INTERNAL_ORGANIZATION_ID
@personId = REPLACE_WITH_PERSON_ID_FROM_CONTACT_RESPONSE
@directoryTenantId = REPLACE_WITH_MEMBER_TOKEN_TID
@objectId = REPLACE_WITH_MEMBER_TOKEN_OID
@membershipId = REPLACE_WITH_MEMBERSHIP_ID_FROM_GRANT_RESPONSE
@systemId = REPLACE_WITH_ASSIGNED_SYSTEM_ID
@administratorAssignmentId = REPLACE_WITH_ADMINISTRATOR_ASSIGNMENT_ID

### Additional verified scoped policy contract (server enforcement required):
### SAP generate/finalize + SAR generate: applicable SCA or ISSM (specs 015/018).
### Task creation: applicable ISSM (Kanban SecurityLead); task movement is ISSM-any
### or ISSO-own and still requires the domain transition/comment/validation checks.
### System role assignment: org Administrator or the exact Feature 049 target matrix.
### Validation links: applicable SCA (spec 069); never inferred from system management.
### Legacy Compliance.Administrator is not automatically an organization Administrator grant.
### Ticketing, deviations, organization capability creation, organization override review,
### and deferred-prerequisite authority remain unavailable pending explicit policy decisions.

### Per-system permissions: effective assignments, never the first/highest persona.
### Applicable overrides replace inherited/org roles; organization Administrator gives
### oversight, not narrative approval or AO decision authority. Membership alone gives none.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/systems/{{systemId}}/workspace-access
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### Bounded portfolio action projection: repeated systemIds, at most 100 input IDs.
### Returns data.items with full role sets and permissions; denied/unknown IDs have canRead=false.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/workspace-access?systemIds={{systemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### Root canCreateSystem requires an active organization ISSM assignment (Feature 015).
### Administrative oversight alone does not imply customer-system authorship or AO authority.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/systems
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Locally verified system","systemType":"MajorApplication","missionCriticality":"MissionSupport"}

### CSP-only separate role enrollment for an existing, actively linked organization Person.
### Membership grant remains a separate operation and creates no RMF/Administrator role.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/administrator-assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: csp
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
Content-Type: application/json

{"personId":"{{personId}}"}

### Follow the enrollment Location with CSP or authorized organization administrator credentials
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/administrator-assignments/{{administratorAssignmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: csp
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### Create an isolation organization without inventing a directory mapping.
### This remains Pending onboarding; it creates neither memberships nor administrator roles.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: csp
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
Content-Type: application/json

{"displayName":"Local test organization"}

### Public login bootstrap: no tenant or membership required
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login-config

### Discover contexts without choosing a browser-global active organization
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/workspaces?page=1&pageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Explicit organization request; homeTenant can be null.
### Cache identity is (data.directoryTenantId, data.oid). directoryTenantId is the
### authenticated subject's directory, never effectiveTenant.id or homeTenant.id.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### CSP operator: find an existing organization-local Person (contact email grants no access)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/membership-persons?query=
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: csp
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### CSP operator: create contact if none exists; creates neither membership nor role
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/membership-persons
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: csp
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
Content-Type: application/json

{"displayName":"Local test member","email":"local-member@example.invalid"}

### CSP or existing organization Administrator: explicit trusted identity association
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/memberships
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: csp
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
Content-Type: application/json

{"directoryTenantId":"{{directoryTenantId}}","objectId":"{{objectId}}","personId":"{{personId}}"}

### List active and revoked grants (CSP context); org admins instead send their organization headers
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/memberships?page=1&pageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: csp
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### Read the resource referenced by a successful grant's Location header
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/memberships/{{membershipId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: csp
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### Revoke; last accessible organization Administrator returns 409 LAST_ADMIN_PROTECTED
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/memberships/{{membershipId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: csp
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### Support entry is separately audited and never creates ordinary membership
### Durable-session contract: new support tokens carry a persisted session ID.
### Every support request/delivery must validate that server-side record; valid
### JWT signatures alone do not authorize workspace support. Missing/revoked rows
### fail closed. Pre-rollout stateless support tokens require a new support entry.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/impersonate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: csp
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### Use the response's HttpOnly cookie through your local HTTP client's cookie jar
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
X-Workspace-Mode: support

### Exit support using CSP scope, including when the support token has expired
### Exit revokes the presented server-side session before clearing its cookie.
### A captured copy replayed by another app instance or existing socket must fail
### on its next authorization check. Other actors/sessions are not implicitly revoked.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/tenants/impersonation
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: csp
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### Negative test: unknown or revoked membership returns 403, never a home-tenant fallback
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
